[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115373,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Middle ear squamous cell carcinoma (MeSCC) is a carcinoma showing squamous differentiation arising from metaplastic squamous epithelium lining the middle ear.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115374,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8070/3 Squamous cell carcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115375,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C21.1 Squamous cell carcinoma of middle ear</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115376,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> epidermoid carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115377,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115378,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) arising primarily in the middle ear is rare. Direct extension from SCC of the pinna, nasopharynx, and/or the sinonasal tract is more common but is not discussed here {32366754} (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/52/301/24237\" target=\"_blank\">#24237</a>Table&nbsp;8.01).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115379,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Presenting findings include hearing loss, otorrhoea, otalgia, bleeding, tinnitus, vertigo, and facial nerve palsy {20513031; 26472473; 23553471; 24121777; 28692593}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115380,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p>MeSCC affects approximately 0.017&nbsp;in 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;individuals {19373882; 25081186; 26472473; 28692593}. The mean age at presentation is 60&nbsp;years (range: 21&ndash;89&nbsp;years), with an equal sex distribution {15925819; 20513031; 24121777}. MeSCC is rarely bilateral {10077254; 11667995}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-12-19T14:42:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115381,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Predisposing factors include chronic otitis media and irradiation {25932267; 31890889}. Viral etiology and genetic alterations (such as <em>DEK</em>::<em>AFF2</em>) have been described {21493437; 32366754}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115382,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115383,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Late presentation is common, with tumour filling the middle ear and extending into mastoid air spaces {15925819; 24121777; 25081186; 26472473; 28692593}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115384,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>The histological features and immunohistochemical profile of MeSCC are similar to those of SCC at other sites, with pleomorphic epithelial cells arranged in sheets with a pavemented appearance, increased N:C&nbsp;ratio, and coarse nuclear chromatin. Most tumours are keratinizing and well to moderately differentiated. Non-keratinizing tumours may be EBV-associated or harbour genetic alterations (such as <em>DEK</em>::<em>AFF2</em> rearrangements) {21493437; 32366754; 34049316}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunoreactivity for pancytokeratin, p40, p63, and CK5/6 is noted.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Direct extension from external ear, nasopharynx, or sinonasal tract tumours should be excluded with clinical and radiological correlation, with EBV-encoded small RNA (EBER), NUT immunohistochemistry, or molecular testing for genetic rearrangements aiding in classification {21493437; 28060373; 34049316; 34108636}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-28T15:17:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115385,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115386,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically performed</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115387,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> an infiltrating squamous epithelial proliferation with malignant cytological and architectural features; clinical exclusion of direct extension from adjacent sites.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-26T16:43:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115388,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p >Staging follows the eighth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system for head and neck cutaneous SCC, although expert-derived modifications are suggested {30500288} [[Thompson LDR, Gupta R, Sandison A, et al. Ear and temporal bone tumours: histopathology reporting guide. 1st ed. Sydney (Australia): International Collaboration on Cancer Reporting; 2018.]].</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-16T17:26:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115389,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 301,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is generally poor because of advanced disease at presentation and delayed diagnosis {31890889}. Outcome is related to stage at presentation {23507994}, and the reported 5-year survival rate is between 25% (for high-volume disease) and 83% (for low-volume disease) {23202152; 23553471; 24121777; 24492135; 26472473}. Direct intracranial extension carries a poor prognosis. Nodal metastases are uncommon, affecting level&nbsp;I and&nbsp;III neck lymph nodes when identified {20513031}; distant metastases are rare.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:28:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]